  "solution": {
    "text": "<blockquote><p>Given,<br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"bold-italic\">p</mi><mo>:</mo></math> Ramesh listens to music.<br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"bold-italic\">q</mi><mo>:</mo></math> Ramesh is out of his village<br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"bold-italic\">r</mi><mo>:</mo></math> It is Sunday<br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"bold-italic\">s</mi><mo mathvariant=\"bold\">:</mo></math> It is Saturday</p><p>Then the statement &quot;Ramesh listens to music only if he is in his village and it is Sunday or Saturday&quot; can be expressed as</p><p>Now on breaking each statement and combining them we get,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>p</mi><mo>&#8801;</mo></math> Ramesh listens to music</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>~</mo><mi>q</mi><mo>&#8801;</mo></math>&nbsp;He is in village.</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>r</mi><mo>&#8744;</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>&#8801;</mo></math> Saturday or Sunday</p><p>So, on combining all statement we get,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>p</mi><mo>&#8658;</mo><mfenced><mrow><mfenced><mrow><mo>~</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>&#8743;</mo><mfenced><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>&#8744;</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></mfenced></mrow></mfenced></math></p></blockquote>",
